From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: explorer: the shell makes its tray settings key

HKCU\Software\Classes\Local Settings\Software\Microsoft\Windows\
CurrentVersion\TrayNotify (where the shell keeps which notification-area
icons show) always exists where a shell has run. Squirrel's installer
(Discord, and other Squirrel-installed programs) reads it with
Registry.GetValue after installing, and a missing key gives it null: a
NullReferenceException in TrayStateChanger.RemoveDeadEntries, the install
aborted, and Discord's installer never returned. The desktop process now
creates the key, before any program can run on the desktop.

Gate: test/commapps-gate.sh.
---
--- a/programs/explorer/desktop.c
+++ b/programs/explorer/desktop.c
@@ -1376,6 +1376,19 @@
     status = NtSetInformationProcess( GetCurrentProcess(), ProcessWineGrantAdminToken, NULL, 0 );
     if (status) WARN( "couldn't set admin token for desktop, error %08lx\n", status );
 
+    /* The shell keeps its notification area's settings (which icons show)
+     * under this key, and it always exists where a shell has run; Squirrel
+     * installers (Discord, Slack's old one, ...) read it when they install
+     * and fail without it. Made before the desktop window, so it is there
+     * by the time any program can run on this desktop. */
+    {
+        HKEY key;
+
+        if (!RegCreateKeyExW( HKEY_CURRENT_USER, L"Software\\Classes\\Local Settings\\Software\\Microsoft\\"
+                              "Windows\\CurrentVersion\\TrayNotify", 0, NULL, 0, KEY_WRITE, NULL, &key, NULL ))
+            RegCloseKey( key );
+    }
+
     /* create the desktop window */
     hwnd = CreateWindowExW( 0, DESKTOP_CLASS_ATOM, NULL,
                             WS_POPUP | WS_CLIPSIBLINGS | WS_CLIPCHILDREN, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, &guid );
